Expected outcome: MALFORMED_XML, quarantined, never published. This is what a feed actually ships
when an export job fails: a status report or a truncated file with an .xml extension. It is not
well-formed XML at all, so the parser never gets far enough to check the schema — which is why the
outcome is MALFORMED_XML rather than SCHEMA_INVALID, and why its diagnostics carry no cvc- code.

